# Tests that are not run by `tests/run.sh --target windows`: "dir/name reason". Everything
# else is built for Windows and run under Wine. Only what is Linux by nature is listed: the
# library tests run on both systems (they work in directories under tmp/ and start
# themselves as child processes), and tests/sys/win_* add the cases only Windows has.
run/lib_args_empty_argv an empty argv (execve with argv = {NULL}) is a Linux situation: a Windows process always has a command line
run/lib_stdout_errors Linux system calls (fork, dup2, fcntl O_NONBLOCK) and /dev/full; a closed standard output on Windows is sys/win_process
std/asset_cloexec Linux close-on-exec of descriptors, seen through a FIFO and /proc/<pid>/fdinfo
std/os the Linux half of the std.os tests: /bin/sh, signals a program sends itself, chmod, `#!` scripts (the portable half: std/os_files, std/os_run, std/os_spawn)
std/window_logic the X11 translation helpers of std.window (key_from_keysym, XEvent accessors) exist only on Linux
sys/window_nodisplay an X11 display name (WindowDesc.display) means nothing on Windows
sys/window_x11 needs an X server (AL_TEST_DISPLAY)
sys/window_x11_events needs an X server (AL_TEST_DISPLAY) and calls Xlib itself
sys/wayland std.wayland is Linux only
sys/audio_alsa_params std.alsa binds libasound.so.2 (Linux)
check/wayland std.wayland is Linux only
check/wayland_window std.wayland is Linux only
sys/vk_triangle std.vk binds libvulkan.so.1 (Linux)
fail/extern on Windows extern functions may take and return structs (Microsoft x64): other diagnostics
sys/shaderc std.shaderc binds libshaderc_shared.so.1 (Linux)
std/vk_glue std.vk binds libvulkan.so.1 (Linux)
sys/vk_renderer std.vk binds libvulkan.so.1 (Linux)
sys/vk_present std.vk binds libvulkan.so.1; std.wayland is Linux only
